WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.632
This query keeps the source table once.

00:00:02.632 --> 00:00:06.627
The lateral VALUES block emits three rows for each product.

00:00:06.627 --> 00:00:11.037
Each generated row contains a sale month and the corresponding revenue.

00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:14.552
Run the query and compare the output with UNION ALL.

00:00:14.552 --> 00:00:18.162
The two forms should represent the same long relationship.

00:00:18.162 --> 00:00:25.637
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:28.917
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:34.892
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:34.892 --> 00:00:35.629
combination.
